I assume (perhaps incorrectly) the question is about putting these
characters onto figures.  Steve's suggestion

> You can generate a superscript "2" in your code by depressing the ALT key
> and typing 253. For mu, use ALT then 230. Just FYI, beta is ALT then 255.

is fairly platform-specific.  Another alternative when preparing postscript
plots is my postscriptfonts package, available from Statlib, which uses
escape sequences embedded in the string to change fonts, sizes, etc.
The only thing that is postscript-specific about it is that it uses
PostScript font metrics to work out the spacing of the groups of
characters; thus it could probably be adapted fairly easily to other
graphics devices.

