Here is a crude function I have used inspired by the g-and-h Distribution 
(seefor example Introduction to Robust Estimation by Rand R.Wilcox) for 
generating skewed data:

goh_function(n,g=0,h=0,p=1,cmat=diag(p)){
tilf_matrix(rnorm(n*p),ncol=p)
if (g>0) tilf2_(exp(g*tilf)-1)/g*exp(0.5*h*tilf^2)
if (g==0) tilf2_tilf*exp(0.5*h*tilf^2)
svcmat_svd(cmat)
cmatsqrt_t(svcmat$v %*% (t(svcmat$u) * sqrt(svcmat$d)))
tilf2_tilf2 %*% cmatsqrt
return(tilf2)
}

apa_goh(100,0,0.5,2)
plot(apa)
c(
cor.test(apa,method="p")$estimate,
cor.test(apa,method="s")$estimate,
cor.test(apa,method="k")$estimate)

p_5
cobs_cs(p,1,.1)
apa_goh(20,0,0,p,cobs)
dimnames(apa)[2]_list(paste("Variable",1:ncol(apa)))
splom(~apa)

p_3
cobs_cs(p,1,.3)
apa_goh(20,0.1,0.1,p,cobs)
dimnames(apa)[2]_list(paste("Variable",1:ncol(apa)))
cobs
cov.wt(apa)$cov
cov.mve(apa)$cov

I hope you might find it useful.

