for a function that undertakes linear clustering as defined by W.D. Fisher,
1958, JASA 53(284)789:798.  I came across this work in the 1970s via papers
by H. Spath, 1973, Computing 11:175-177, and R. Bellman, 1973, Mathematical
Biosciences 18:311-312.  As a result I (still) have CDC Cyber Fortran code
that I implemented at that time.  A similar problem as the one I was
tackling then has arisen.  Before I start working on an S+ script (6.1 v1
under Win 2K) I thought it would be sensible to cast my net acroos the
ever-helpful community and see if a script was out there already.

To those with a cartographic bent, this is the procedure known as Natural
Breaks in ESRI's ArcView.  There are two procedures in the cartography
community, Jenks-Caspall and Fisher-Jenks; the latter appeals to me more as
it is robust and that is the script that I am after.  For those interested
there is a discussion of these in T. Slocum's 1999, Prentice-Hall book,
Thematic Cartography and Visualization.

Any help would be appreciated,

