     What do you mean by "product"?  The moment generating function / 
characteristic function of a sum of two random variables is the product 
of the moment generating / characteristic functions.  I think I've seen 
"convolution" described as a "product", more or less for this reason. 

     Have you looked in the Johnson and Kotz volumes on distributions 
in statistics?  Many of the chapters contain sections on "related 
distributions", etc. 

     More generally, what problem are you trying to solve?  Why do you 
ask this question?  If we know more about that, we may be able to 
provide more useful comments? 

