Message-ID: <200310081752.h98HqEt27756@prolapse.mayo.edu>

  No one has mentioned the simplest solution to these problems, which is
just to dispose of factors entirely.

     > options(stringsAsFactors=F)  # force S to stop auto conversions
     > tuss$site <- as.character(tuss$site)

  Now you no longer have to deal with the "features" of site as a factor.

  [Soapbox on] 
     This approach is almost always met by some replys that "turning factors
off might break some features of Splus".  Well, we've had them turned off
by default in our 100+ user base for 10+ years now (actually, ever since they
first appeared), and nothing has shown up yet.  Factors are ocassionaly
useful, and one can always create one explicitly with factor(x).  The default
action of turning every character string into a factor is a plague on the
S language.
  [Soapbox off]

For older versions of S there is no global option, but you 
can turn off the behavior for data frames at least wtth
     > as.data.frame.character <- as.data.frame.vector

Fixing the problem in R is quite a bit trickier, since if function f1()
calls f2(), and you later find and fix a bug in f2, the fix does not
get recognized by f1 until you re-source it as well. 

        Terry Therneau

From andy_liaw at merck.com  Wed Oct  8 18:56:51 2003
From: andy_liaw at merck.com (Liaw, Andy)
