"Something else" that can be quite useful, in both S-plus and R, is to 
store the data with the model.  This will increase object size, but it 
removes uncertainty about where the data might be coming from.  Many model 
objects allow this, but some of them do not support it through 
specification of arguments (or document it) -- you have to read the code to 
see how the functions are looking for data, and then assign model 
components directly.   For example, in tree objects, I believe that one can 
assign the model frame to the tree after building it, like this:

  fitted.tree <- tree(...) # however you would normally fit the tree
  fitted.tree$model <- tree(..., method="model.frame")

Now, cv.tree(fitted.tree) will use the data stored in the "model" component 
of fitted.tree.

If anyone knows of gotchas in this way of doing things, please advise!

Tony Plate

