----- Original Message -----
From: Steve McKinney
To: Steve Su
Sent: Tuesday, October 14, 2003 5:26 AM
Subject: RE: [S] Attaching large amoung of graphics into Word

Hi Steve,

Here is an example of a macro I defined to pull all graphs named wmfpc??.wmf
into my word doc.

I have an S-PLUS script that generates pages of graphs into these numbered
wmfpc??.wmf files (wmfpc01.wmf, wmfpc02.wmf, ...)

The number of output graphs changes all the time, so I do not know a-priori
how many graphs I need to pull into word.

So, in Word, I just run this macro, and all the files are pulled in
automatically.

-------------------------------------------------
GetAllPearsonBarGraphs macro:
-------------------------------------------------
Public Sub MAIN()
Dim size_
Dim count_

WordBasic.FileFind Name:="wmfpc??.wmf"
size_ = WordBasic.CountFoundFiles() - 1
If size_ >= 0 Then
 For count_ = 0 To size_

  WordBasic.InsertPicture Name:=WordBasic.[FoundFileName$](count_ + 1),
LinkToFile:="0"
  WordBasic.EndOfDocument

 Next
Else
 WordBasic.MsgBox "Couldn't find any files  wmfpc*.wmf  in this directory."
End If

End Sub

