David,
   I think what you're missing is in the sapply call. In S-PLUS you need 
to supply the variables explicitly.

indicator <- paste( "foo.2$X <- sapply(foo.2$id, FUN = function(x, X) 
if(x == X) 1 else 0, X = X)" )

Before, I don't think S-PLUS knew how to evaluate "X". In R, "X" is 
found by the scoping rules.

I haven't tested this, but it's a common mistake.

-sundar

