 Have you considered "survReg", as described in, e.g., Venables and
Ripley (2002) Modern Applied Statistics with S (Springer)?

I don't understand your problem. The likelihood for an observed event is
the density, while for a censored event is the probability of occurrence
in the interval. This probability (density) depends on the parameter(s),
but time(s) do not. I've done this in Excel, S-Plus, R, etc.

If you provide a very simple toy example, someone might be able to help
more.

Also, I would not use nlminb for this. If survReg won't solve your
problem, I'd try optim in library(MASS).

hope this helps.
spencer graves

