Here is one way of doing it.  I have a matrix with the data you provided
and use that to 'sample' a selection of indices to see which of the entries
gets a '1'.  "sample" has a 'prob' parameter that says what it the
probability of selecting that value.

After selecting the proper indices, we can set the value in the 'x.result'
matrix:

> x.1
     [,1] [,2] [,3] [,4]
[1,]    2  0.3  0.2  0.5
[2,]    2  0.5  0.4  0.1
[3,]    1  0.1  0.1  0.8
[4,]    1  0.7  0.2  0.1
[5,]    2  0.8  0.1  0.1
> # create samples from data in the matrix
> x.index <- apply(x.1, 1, function(x) sample(1:3, x[1], prob=x[2:4]))
> # create the result matrix
> x.result <- matrix(0, ncol=3, nrow=nrow(x.1))
> # set the appropriate entries to 1
> invisible(lapply(1:nrow(x.1), function(x) x.result[x, x.index[[x]]] <<-
1))
> x.result
     [,1] [,2] [,3]
[1,]    1    0    1
[2,]    1    1    0
[3,]    1    0    0
[4,]    1    0    0
[5,]    1    1    0
>

