From ezivot at u.washington.edu  Sun Oct 19 19:25:32 2003
From: ezivot at u.washington.edu (Eric Zivot)
Date: Sun, 19 Oct 2003 12:25:32 -0700
Subject: Re: [splus] granger causality
In-Reply-To: <20031019061303.270D44021AB@smtp.biostat.wustl.edu>
References: <20031019061303.270D44021AB@smtp.biostat.wustl.edu>
Message-ID: <004001c39676$c3ea85e0$6401a8c0@zivotd800>

I describe how to do Granger Causality tests in my book Modeling Financial
Time Series with S-Plus. Bivariate GC tests are simple (just an F test for
zero values of lagged regressors) and can be done using lm. Multivariate GC
tests generally require fitting a vector autoregressive model. This can also
be done with lm since lm can fit a multivariate (more than one dependent
variable) regression. The FinMetrics module from Insightful has functions
for fitting VAR models and this greatly reduces the work involved in
computing GC tests. ez

